/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T ( Sterilization : Eliminating Microorganisms! After decontamination, the instruments are sterilized to eliminate harmful microorganisms, including bacteria, viruses, and spores. CSSD uses various sterilization methods tailored to the material and nature of the instruments as indicated below: Steam Sterilization: This high-temperature process is used for heat-resistant instruments, ensuring effective microbial deactivation. Ethylene Oxide Sterilization: For delicate items that cannot withstand steam, ethylene oxide gas is used to sterilize instruments. Hydrogen Peroxide Plasma Sterilization: This method is employed for delicate equipment, using low-temperature vapor to sterilize effectively.)
/E ( Sterilization : Eliminating Microorganisms! After decontamination, the instruments are sterilized to eliminate harmful microorganisms, including bacteria, viruses, and spores. CSSD uses various sterilization methods tailored to the material and nature of the instruments as indicated below: Steam Sterilization: This high-temperature process is used for heat-resistant instruments, ensuring effective microbial deactivation. Ethylene Oxide Sterilization: For delicate items that cannot withstand steam, ethylene oxide gas is used to sterilize instruments. Hydrogen Peroxide Plasma Sterilization: This method is employed for delicate equipment, using low-temperature vapor to sterilize effectively.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Assembly and Packaging: Maintaining Sterility! Once sterilized, instruments are carefully assembled into sets for specific surgical procedures, then packaged in sterile containers or wraps to maintain their sterility until use. CSSD ensures that these packages are sealed, labeled, and ready for distribution.)
/E (Assembly and Packaging: Maintaining Sterility! Once sterilized, instruments are carefully assembled into sets for specific surgical procedures, then packaged in sterile containers or wraps to maintain their sterility until use. CSSD ensures that these packages are sealed, labeled, and ready for distribution.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
