/E (The Department of Psycho-oncology, Cancer Institute \(WIA\), conducted multiple awareness programs across schools, colleges, and communities, reaching thousands. Key initiatives included student interventions, tobacco cessation programs, oral cancer screenings, and interactive workshops using play-based methods. Special events like National Cancer Awareness Day and International Volunteers Day engaged students, shopkeepers, and professionals in tobacco-free initiatives and hair donations for cancer patients. A Tobacco-Free Educational Institute Initiative was launched, alongside awareness stalls and online training for healthcare professionals. )
