283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Where there is a will, there is a way. This timeless wisdom defines the inspiring journey of G.K. Rangarajan from our Nuclear Medicine department, whose relentless pursuit of knowledge embodies perseverance.  Rangarajan began his career in 1988 at KJ Hospital after completing his Plus Two, undertaking CRA training while working in Nuclear Medicine. His thirst for learning led him to earn a B.Sc. in Physics from Madras University \(2003\) and later an M.Sc. from Annamalai University \(2008\), all through correspondence. In 2005, he joined our Institute as a Nuclear Medicine Technologist, bringing both experience and an unyielding desire for growth.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
